## Исправление раздельных очередей (Промт для Aider):

Промт:
Excellent! The safety check caught the bug. The reason graphicsQueue is null is because on this hybrid GPU system, graphics operations and window presentation are handled by TWO DIFFERENT queue families. We must implement support for separate queue families.
Modify main.cpp as follows:

   1. In the class private members, replace uint32_t graphicsQueueFamilyIndex with two distinct variables:
   * int graphicsFamilyIndex = -1;
      * int presentFamilyIndex = -1;
      Also add a new queue handle: VkQueue presentQueue = VK_NULL_HANDLE;.
   2. In pickPhysicalDevice(), rewrite the queue family loop. For each family index i:
   * If queueFlags & VK_QUEUE_GRAPHICS_BIT, set graphicsFamilyIndex = i;.
      * Check presentation support using VkBool32 presentSupport = VK_FALSE; vkGetPhysicalDeviceSurfaceSupportKHR(device, i, surface, &presentSupport);. If presentSupport, set presentFamilyIndex = i;.
      * Break the loop only when BOTH graphicsFamilyIndex >= 0 and presentFamilyIndex >= 0.
   3. In createLogicalDevice(), if graphicsFamilyIndex != presentFamilyIndex, you must create TWO VkDeviceQueueCreateInfo structures (one for each index) instead of one, and pass them as an array to VkDeviceCreateInfo. If they are the same, just pass one.
   4. After successfully creating the logical device, retrieve both queue handles:
   * vkGetDeviceQueue(device, graphicsFamilyIndex, 0, &graphicsQueue);
      * vkGetDeviceQueue(device, presentFamilyIndex, 0, &presentQueue);
   5. In createSwapChain(), look at createInfo.imageSharingMode. If graphicsFamilyIndex != presentFamilyIndex:
   * Set createInfo.imageSharingMode = VK_SHARING_MODE_CONCURRENT;
      * Set createInfo.queueFamilyIndexCount = 2;
      * Pass an array containing both indices: uint32_t queueFamilyIndices[] = {static_cast<uint32_t>(graphicsFamilyIndex), static_cast<uint32_t>(presentFamilyIndex)}; createInfo.pQueueFamilyIndices = queueFamilyIndices;
      * Otherwise, keep it VK_SHARING_MODE_EXCLUSIVE.
   6. Update createCommandPool() to use graphicsFamilyIndex.

