## Исправление порядка вызовов (Промт для Aider):

Промт:
Look at your createLogicalDevice() method in main.cpp. You have a critical sequencing bug: you are calling vkGetDeviceQueue BEFORE calling vkCreateDevice! You cannot retrieve a queue from a device that hasn't been created yet.
Fix the order of execution inside createLogicalDevice() strictly as follows:

   1. First, set up the VkDeviceQueueCreateInfo and VkDeviceCreateInfo structures using graphicsQueueFamilyIndex.
   2. Second, call vkCreateDevice(physicalDevice, &createInfo, nullptr, &device). Ensure you check that it returns VK_SUCCESS.
   3. Third, ONLY AFTER vkCreateDevice succeeds, call vkGetDeviceQueue(device, graphicsQueueFamilyIndex, 0, &graphicsQueue);.
   4. Move the debug print std::cout << "vkGetDeviceQueue executed. Handle address: " << graphicsQueue << std::endl; to be the very last line of createLogicalDevice(), right after you successfully retrieve the queue.

